    "carrier_of_transfer": "antecedent chl-a persistence (temporal autocorrelation of biomass) \u2014 a universal property \u2014 NOT instantaneous satellite optics + drivers, which transfer only weakly on their own (see fusion_no_antecedent_chl).",
    "conclusion": "YES \u2014 the physically-driven chl-a bloom anomaly transfers cross-region (fusion AUROC 0.62-0.65, region-clustered bootstrap CI excludes 0.5; antecedent-chl-alone 0.78-0.79) whereas microcystin collapses to chance (~0.49-0.54) on the SAME 3 coherent regions (CA, HUC30, HUC31). BUT the transfer is carried by ANTECEDENT chl-a PERSISTENCE (temporal autocorrelation of biomass \u2014 a universal property), NOT by the satellite+driver instantaneous physics originally hypothesised: those alone are AT chance cross-region (0.47-0.50) and, when added, DILUTE the antecedent signal (full fusion 0.62-0.65 < antecedent-alone 0.78). Honest verdict: fusion generalises OOD here, but not for the hypothesised reason."
